-- target: branch
--
-- LEVEL THE REHEARSAL BRANCH WITH MAIN'S 292 SHARING-REGISTRY ROWS.
--
-- WHY
-- ---
-- `platform.shareable_resource_registry` is the platform's list of what can be SHARED and under
-- which token. `iam.has_access` reads it, and a CHECK on `permissions` refuses a grant whose
-- `resource_type` is not one of its rows, in as many words:
--
--   permissions.resource_type=record is not a registered sharing TOKEN. Pass the entity token
--   (platform.entity_types.token = shareable_resource_registry.resource_type) — a table name here
--   would be stored and then silently ignored by iam.has_access, which is the bug this guard kills.
--
-- Main carries 292 rows including `record`. The rehearsal branch, after the first live
-- BRANCH-REFRESH, carried ZERO: nothing holds a foreign key to this table, so the refresh's
-- catalog-derived seed set could not see it — the same blind spot that left
-- `platform.deprecated_relations` and `custom.carrying_rule` empty.
--
-- With it empty, every store path that grants or checks access died at the CHECK, and the doors
-- downstream answered the honest-but-misleading `You do not have access to this table, so
-- custom.table_capacity has nothing to show you` — 19 of lane RECORDS-SUITE-2's branch failures,
-- reading as an access regression in the record store when the registry simply was not there.
--
-- THE CLASS FIX IS IN THE REFRESH: `scripts/night/branch-refresh.sh` now names this table in
-- `NAMED_REGISTRIES`. This file is the instance fix so the store's suite can be classified today.
--
-- NO CUSTOMER DATA. All 292 rows belong to the ONE `is_system` organization
-- (39c38960-d30c-4840-b0c1-c9960de95582, "Matrx System"), which is exactly the filter the refresh
-- itself applies, and `created_by`/`updated_by` are NULL on every one of them on main — so the two
-- `auth.users` foreign keys cannot bind to a purged identity. `created_at`/`updated_at` are left
-- to the branch's own defaults rather than carrying main's timestamps.
--
-- ADDITIVE and idempotent: one INSERT … SELECT over a jsonb payload, `on conflict (resource_type)
-- do nothing`. No DDL, no DROP, no REVOKE, no function replaced.
--
-- lane: RECORDS-SUITE-2

